From 93c98a842bb1941b8d20735c255f88577cdf8b9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Remora <noreply@localhost>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 19:58:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Support the VAAPI HEVC encoder path

Extend the shared V4L2/C2 encoder scaffolding so the out-of-tree VAAPI
HEVC encoder (hardware/remora/c2-va) can drive it end to end:

- EncodeInterface: add an HEVC branch (was H264/VP8/VP9 only) with
  HEVCProfileLevelSetter; raise kMaxBitrate from ~50 Mbps (AVC L4.1) so
  high daily-driver bitrates (150 Mbps) aren't silently rejected back to
  the 64 kbps default; tag input-stream usage with C2MemoryUsage::CPU_READ
  so gralloc allocates the encoder input surface linear (minigbm would
  otherwise pick an X-tiled layout the VAAPI DRM_PRIME import misreads).
- EncodeComponent: skip the gralloc FormatConverter when the encoder
  reports handlesInputFormatConversion() (the VAAPI core VPP-converts).
- VideoEncoder: add the handlesInputFormatConversion() hook.
- EncodeHelpers: extract HEVC VPS/SPS/PPS in extractCSDInfo so the mirror
  gets a proper codec-config packet for H.265 streams.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I39298fa7d446ba34b40a69234b7ab7979c1674d3
